# The keys' half of the check that an action leads where its key leads (scripts\verify\panel.ps1, part actions): this
# file reaches a state by keys, tests\window-actions.input the same state by actions, each run live in a window:
#   RayTracingViewer cornell -w 320 --height 180 -s 32 --input tests\window-actions-keys.input --record r.txt
# The two recordings must hold the same settings in the same order (their lines other than frames, which the clock
# doesn't change), end on the same frame, and P's files must be the same bytes. Every key waits 20 frames for the
# image before it to be done; two keys at one frame step twice with no frame between, so the recording shows only
# where they led.
#
# M, M: from the Cornell box's own strategy past uniform to material
at 20 key M
at 20 key M
# T, T: from the books' bytes past none to agx; then a stop of exposure up, in two half stops
at 40 key T
at 40 key T
at 60 key .
at 60 key .
# Shift+Tab: the scene before cornell, light, which takes material along
at 80 key-down Left Shift
at 80 key Tab
at 80 key-up Left Shift
# F2: refused, agx computes in float32 only
at 100 key F2
# Enter: 32 samples asked for, rounded up to a round of 64 and doubled: 128
at 120 key Return
# ]: the lens opens to a quarter of a degree; R: back to the start view; =: the field of view times 0.9, 20 to 18
at 160 key ]
at 180 key R
at 200 key =
# Space, Space: paused, and on again
at 220 key Space
at 230 key Space
# P: the image saved once it is done, as light-view-001.png and .pfm, with its command
at 300 key P
at 320 quit
